<Folder><name>Gyeongui Line Forest Park walk (경의선숲길)</name>
<Placemark><name>Yeontral Park → Hongik Univ. Stn → Book Street → Seogang sky bridge, 2.7 km</name><description><![CDATA[2.7 km<br>1. Official course line from Naver Map (마포걷고싶은길 1코스 · 경의선숲길), Gajwa → Seogang section]]></description><styleUrl>#line-0</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>126.914653,37.568333,0 126.915215,37.568113,0 126.915771,37.567889,0 126.916084,37.567746,0 126.916625,37.567467,0 126.916825,37.567358,0 126.917025,37.567233,0 126.917150,37.567167,0 126.917212,37.567142,0 126.917475,37.567066,0 126.917622,37.567030,0 126.917801,37.567308,0 126.918182,37.567139,0 126.918476,37.566989,0 126.918728,37.566854,0 126.919084,37.566641,0 126.919201,37.566536,0 126.919455,37.566293,0 126.919502,37.566234,0 126.919652,37.565867,0 126.919798,37.565668,0 126.919890,37.565572,0 126.919988,37.565514,0 126.920158,37.565424,0 126.920249,37.565364,0 126.920374,37.565213,0 126.920454,37.565106,0 126.920542,37.564942,0 126.920658,37.564645,0 126.920760,37.564496,0 126.921101,37.564060,0 126.921233,37.563944,0 126.921458,37.563772,0 126.921869,37.563270,0 126.922044,37.563026,0 126.922116,37.562809,0 126.922515,37.562304,0 126.923118,37.561795,0 126.923229,37.561627,0 126.923460,37.561118,0 126.923689,37.560834,0 126.923744,37.560777,0 126.924110,37.560569,0 126.924151,37.560523,0 126.924189,37.560475,0 126.924244,37.560360,0 126.924339,37.560221,0 126.924473,37.559866,0 126.924617,37.559672,0 126.924960,37.559439,0 126.925782,37.558373,0 126.925662,37.558283,0 126.925798,37.558132,0 126.926324,37.557670,0 126.926494,37.557411,0 126.926661,37.557314,0 126.926832,37.557204,0 126.926973,37.557346,0 126.927541,37.557024,0 126.928093,37.556761,0 126.929073,37.556338,0 126.929447,37.556250,0 126.929723,37.556072,0 126.930115,37.555942,0 126.930295,37.555868,0 126.930595,37.555642,0 126.930840,37.555506,0 126.931595,37.554996,0 126.931705,37.554837,0 126.931868,37.554722,0 126.932400,37.554424,0 126.932614,37.554287,0 126.932823,37.554126,0 126.932902,37.553998,0 126.932978,37.553920,0 126.933081,37.553832,0 126.933300,37.553755,0 126.933465,37.553713,0 126.933653,37.553623,0 126.934076,37.553313,0 126.934176,37.553031,0 126.934315,37.552925,0 126.934383,37.552862,0 126.934422,37.552820,0 126.934447,37.552775,0 126.934476,37.552698,0 126.934523,37.552630,0 126.935131,37.552202,0 126.935412,37.552375,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Start – Gajwa Station, north end of Yeontral Park</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Start – Gajwa Station, north end of Yeontral Park (가좌역)</b><br>Gyeongui–Jungang line. Exit 1 and walk south-east into the park; the first stretch runs beside the stream to Yeonnam-dong. If you prefer a shorter walk, start at Hongik Univ. Station exit 3 instead (1.3 km in).<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/11636479?lng=126.9146534&lat=37.5683333&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1574-0F9D58</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.914653,37.568333,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Yeontral Park – Yeonnam-dong section</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Yeontral Park – Yeonnam-dong section (연트럴파크 · 경의선숲길)</b><br>The lawn-and-stream stretch everyone picnics on; cafés and bakeries on both sides. Busiest at weekends and in the evening.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/37992172?lng=126.9229820&lat=37.5619570&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1720-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.922982,37.561957,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Hongik University Station exit 3</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Hongik University Station exit 3 (홍대입구역 3번출구)</b><br>Lines 2, Gyeongui–Jungang and AREX. The park passes under the big road here; cross with the lights and continue on the other side.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/21405143?lng=126.9252500&lat=37.5585710&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1719-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.925250,37.558571,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Gyeongui Line Book Street</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Gyeongui Line Book Street (경의선책거리)</b><br>250 m of book kiosks shaped like train carriages, benches and small publishers' stalls; most open from about 11:00, closed Mondays.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1216738398?lng=126.9289900&lat=37.5563600&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1664-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.928990,37.556360,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Ddaengddaeng-geori crossing</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Ddaengddaeng-geori crossing (홍대 땡땡거리)</b><br>Named after the old railway crossing bell; a short lane of bars and restaurants where the line used to cross Wausan-ro.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1643536604?lng=126.9314070&lat=37.5546900&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1611-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.931407,37.554690,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Seogang Station</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Seogang Station (서강대역)</b><br>Gyeongui–Jungang line, right beside the park.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/31375707?lng=126.9354450&lat=37.5521670&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1719-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.935445,37.552167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* End – Seogang sky bridge, start of the bridge</name><description><![CDATA[<b>End – Seogang sky bridge, start of the bridge (서강하늘다리 시작점)</b><br>The footbridge that carries the park over Seogang-ro next to Seogang Station. The park continues south-east to Gongdeok if you want another 1.5 km.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8%ED%8A%B9%EB%B3%84%EC%8B%9C%20%EB%A7%88%ED%8F%AC%EA%B5%AC%20%EC%84%9C%EA%B0%95%EB%A1%9C%20118">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1661-DB4437</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.935412,37.552375,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Red Road – busking street (홍대 레드로드)</name>
<Placemark><name>Red Road busking street: Hongik Univ. Stn exit 9 → Eoulmadang-ro → Red Road stage → Han River, 1.9 km</name><description><![CDATA[1.9 km<br>1. Official course line from Naver Map (홍대 레드로드, main spine R1–R7)]]></description><styleUrl>#line-1</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>126.925021,37.556253,0 126.924729,37.556170,0 126.924525,37.556061,0 126.924297,37.555844,0 126.923970,37.555676,0 126.923793,37.555590,0 126.923562,37.555417,0 126.923351,37.555218,0 126.923311,37.555164,0 126.923146,37.554916,0 126.923050,37.554790,0 126.922969,37.554701,0 126.922876,37.554614,0 126.922754,37.554531,0 126.922550,37.554445,0 126.922462,37.554400,0 126.922600,37.554289,0 126.922536,37.554216,0 126.922012,37.553433,0 126.921925,37.553250,0 126.921787,37.552908,0 126.921630,37.552389,0 126.921561,37.551958,0 126.921415,37.551901,0 126.921389,37.551748,0 126.921301,37.551329,0 126.921189,37.550852,0 126.921048,37.550201,0 126.920986,37.550010,0 126.920687,37.549321,0 126.920450,37.548817,0 126.920196,37.548340,0 126.919958,37.547848,0 126.919918,37.547757,0 126.919558,37.547039,0 126.919248,37.546400,0 126.918924,37.545814,0 126.918759,37.545486,0 126.918728,37.545364,0 126.917884,37.545420,0 126.917519,37.545428,0 126.917367,37.545454,0 126.917223,37.545012,0 126.917427,37.545034,0 126.917590,37.545030,0 126.917619,37.544747,0 126.917644,37.544664,0 126.917682,37.544609,0 126.917994,37.544283,0 126.918417,37.543790,0 126.919091,37.542947,0 126.919173,37.542619,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Start – Hongik University Station exit 9</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Start – Hongik University Station exit 9 (홍대입구역 9번출구)</b><br>Lines 2, Gyeongui–Jungang and AREX. Exit 9 opens straight onto the busking street; the crowds start here from late afternoon.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1392358598?lng=126.9229630&lat=37.5560250&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1574-0F9D58</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.922963,37.556025,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Busking zone – Hongdae Walking Street</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Busking zone – Hongdae Walking Street (홍대 걷고싶은거리 · 레드로드 R1)</b><br>The main busking stretch along Eoulmadang-ro: dance crews and singers most evenings, biggest on Friday and Saturday nights. Street food and the Hongdae Playground on the right.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/18785281?lng=126.9231920&lat=37.5550580&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1535-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.923192,37.555058,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Red Road stage &amp; art centre</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Red Road stage &amp; art centre (레드로드)</b><br>Mid-point of the Red Road, a 2023 pedestrian-first redesign of Hongdae's streets in red paving. Performance stages and the Red Road art lab are around here; Sangsu Station is 200 m east.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1285117041?lng=126.9213110&lat=37.5507170&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1611-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.921311,37.550717,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Sangsu Station</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sangsu Station (상수역)</b><br>Line 6, a short detour east of the route. Cafés of Sangsu-dong are between here and the river.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/13479524?lng=126.9223050&lat=37.5477660&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1719-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.922305,37.547766,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* End – Mapo Saebit Culture Forest and the Han River</name><description><![CDATA[<b>End – Mapo Saebit Culture Forest and the Han River (마포새빛문화숲)</b><br>The Red Road ends at the riverside park by the old Danginri power station, now a cultural park, with the Han River cycle path beyond. Hapjeong Station (lines 2 and 6) is 10 min north-west.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1349999930?lng=126.9181240&lat=37.5440360&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1661-DB4437</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.918124,37.544036,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
</Document></kml>
